# 🚀 AI-Powered Customer Churn & Revenue Intelligence Platform

An end-to-end data analytics and machine learning project that predicts customer churn, identifies at-risk customers, and estimates potential revenue exposure using Python, machine learning, and Power BI.

## 📌 Project Overview

Customer churn is a major challenge for subscription-based businesses. This project analyzes customer behavior, predicts churn probability, identifies important churn drivers, and supports data-driven customer retention strategies.

The platform combines data engineering, exploratory data analysis (EDA), machine learning, explainable AI, revenue risk analysis, and business intelligence.

## 🎯 Project Objectives

- Predict customers who are likely to churn.
- Identify important factors associated with customer churn.
- Segment customers by churn risk.
- Estimate monthly and annual revenue at risk.
- Recommend customer retention actions.
- Present business insights through an interactive Power BI dashboard.

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

| Category | Tools |
|---|---|
| Programming | Python |
| Data Analysis | Pandas, NumPy |
| Visualization | Matplotlib, Seaborn |
| Machine Learning | Scikit-learn, XGBoost |
| Explainable AI | SHAP |
| Business Intelligence | Microsoft Power BI |
| Data Processing | Python, CSV |
| Version Control | Git, GitHub |

## 📊 Dataset

This project uses the IBM Telco Customer Churn dataset.

- **Total customers:** 7,043
- **Customers who churned:** 1,869
- **Customers who did not churn:** 5,174
- **Overall churn rate:** 26.54%

The dataset contains customer demographics, services, contract types, tenure, monthly charges, and churn status.

## 🔎 Key Analytical Insights

The exploratory analysis identified several patterns:

- **Contract type:** Month-to-month customers have a higher churn rate than customers with longer-term contracts.
- **Tenure:** Customers with shorter tenure show higher churn rates.
- **Internet service:** Fiber optic customers have a higher observed churn rate than DSL customers in this dataset.
- **Retention opportunities:** Customers with elevated churn risk can be prioritized for targeted retention campaigns.

These findings describe patterns in the dataset and do not necessarily establish causation.

## 🤖 Machine Learning Model

An XGBoost classification pipeline was trained to predict customer churn.

### Model Performance

| Metric | Score |
|---|---:|
| Accuracy | 79.42% |
| Precision | 64.38% |
| Recall | 50.27% |
| F1-score | 56.46% |
| ROC-AUC | 83.66% |

The ROC-AUC score indicates that the model can distinguish between churn and non-churn customers reasonably well. Recall can be improved further to identify more customers who eventually churn.

## 🧠 Explainable AI

SHAP was used to help explain model predictions and understand which features contribute to churn predictions.

The project includes visual outputs for:
- SHAP summary analysis.
- SHAP feature importance.

## 💰 Revenue Intelligence

The revenue risk analysis categorizes customers into high-, medium-, and low-risk groups.

| Indicator | Result |
|---|---:|
| High-risk customers | 730 |
| Medium-risk customers | 1,292 |
| Low-risk customers | 5,021 |
| Estimated monthly revenue exposure | $139,030.10 |
| Estimated annual revenue exposure | $1,668,361.17 |

**Important:** Revenue exposure is an estimate based on the project's methodology. It represents potential exposure, not confirmed revenue loss or guaranteed savings.

## 📈 Power BI Dashboard

The Power BI dashboard presents key business metrics and customer segments, including:

- Churn rate.
- Monthly and annual revenue at risk.
- Customer churn by contract type.
- Customer distribution by churn risk.
- Retention priority analysis.
- Customer distribution by internet service.

Dashboard file:

`Business_Intelligence/AI_Customer_Churn_Revenue_Intelligence.pbix`

Download the repository to open the dashboard in Microsoft Power BI Desktop.

